# 📖 Introduction

Linux running processes ke sath communicate karne ke liye **signals** ka istemal karta hai.

Is lab mein hum do important signals par focus karenge:

- `SIGINT`
- `SIGHUP`

Hum `nohup` command bhi seekhenge jo process ko terminal band hone ke baad bhi chalne deta hai.

---

# Is Lab Mein Cover Hone Wale Main Signals

| Signal | Common Number | Purpose |
|---------|--------------:|----------|
| `SIGINT` | `2` | Process ko interrupt karna, aam tor par `Ctrl + C` ke zariye |
| `SIGHUP` | `1` | Process ko batana ke uska controlling terminal band ho gaya hai |

> Signal numbers Linux systems par standard hote hain. Agar verify karna ho to `kill -l` command use karein.

