# 9. `pstree` Se Process Tree Dekhna

Run karein:

```bash
pstree -p 2548
```

Kuch systems par yeh process aur uske child processes dikhata hai.

Current shell aur uske child processes dekhne ke liye:

```bash
pstree -p $$
```

Yahan:

```text
$$
```

current shell ka PID represent karta hai.

Example Output:

```text
bash(2400)───sleep(2548)
```

Iska matlab hai ke `sleep` process Bash shell ne start kiya hai.

