# 15. Recommended `nohup` Syntax

Agar command ya script output generate karti ho to recommended syntax yeh hai:

```bash
nohup ./backup.sh > /tmp/backup.log 2>&1 &
```

### Explanation

| Part | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `nohup` | `SIGHUP` ignore kare |
| `./backup.sh` | Script ya command |
| `> /tmp/backup.log` | Standard output log file mein save kare |
| `2>&1` | Standard error bhi usi log file mein bheje |
| `&` | Background mein run kare |

---

# Example – Infinite Logging Loop

Run karein:

```bash
nohup bash -c 'while true; do echo "Process still running at $(date)"; sleep 5; done' > /tmp/nohup-test.log 2>&1 &
```

Ab latest background process ka PID dekhein:

```bash
echo $!
```

Yahan:

```text
$!
```

sab se recently start hone wale background process ka PID return karta hai.

