# 19. Normal Background Job Aur `nohup` Mein Difference

| Feature | `command &` | `nohup command &` |
|----------|-------------|-------------------|
| Background mein run karta hai | Yes | Yes |
| Terminal free rehta hai | Yes | Yes |
| `SIGHUP` ignore karta hai | Zaroori nahi | Yes |
| Logout ke baad survive karta hai | Guarantee nahi | Aksar karta hai |
| Output | Terminal par | `nohup.out` ya redirected file |
| Best Use | Choti background jobs | Long-running jobs jo logout ke baad bhi chalni chahiye |

---

# 20. `nohup`, `screen`, `tmux`, Aur `systemd`

| Tool | Best Use |
|------|----------|
| `nohup` | Simple non-interactive command jo logout ke baad bhi chalni chahiye |
| `screen` | Persistent interactive terminal session |
| `tmux` | Modern terminal multiplexer |
| `systemd` | Production services aur long-running managed processes |

Production environment mein aam tor par **systemd** ko prefer kiya jata hai kyun ke yeh provide karta hai:

- Automatic restart
- Logging
- Dependency management
- Boot ke waqt automatic startup
- Resource controls
- Service status monitoring

