# 🔧 Troubleshooting Scenarios

## Scenario 1 – `Ctrl + C` Process Ko Stop Nahi Kar Raha

Ho sakta hai application `SIGINT` ko handle ya ignore kar rahi ho.

Pehle graceful termination try karein:

```bash
kill -TERM PID
```

Agar phir bhi process terminate na ho:

```bash
kill -KILL PID
```

---

## Scenario 2 – Background Job SSH Disconnect Ke Baad Band Ho Jati Hai

Is tarah start karein:

```bash
nohup command > output.log 2>&1 &
```

Interactive sessions ke liye:

```text
screen
```

ya

```text
tmux
```

use karein.

---

## Scenario 3 – PID Nahi Mil Raha

Commands:

```bash
jobs -l
```

ya

```bash
pgrep -af command_name
```

ya

```bash
ps aux | grep '[c]ommand_name'
```

---

## Scenario 4 – `nohup.out` File Create Ho Gayi

Yeh bilkul normal hai.

Output dekhne ke liye:

```bash
tail -f nohup.out
```

Agar custom file use karni ho:

```bash
nohup command > custom.log 2>&1 &
```

---

## Scenario 5 – `nohup` Ke Bawajood Process Terminate Ho Gaya

Possible reasons:

- Application khud error ki wajah se exit ho gayi.
- Server reboot ho gaya.
- Kisi ne `SIGTERM` ya `SIGKILL` bheja.
- Application terminal input par depend karti thi.
- OOM Killer ne process terminate kar diya.
- Administrator ne manually stop kar diya.

Check karein:

```bash
ps -p PID
```

Aur logs:

```bash
journalctl
```

Aur redirected log file bhi review karein.

