# 📖 Key Takeaways

- `SIGINT` foreground process ko interrupt karta hai.
- `Ctrl + C` normally `SIGINT` bhejta hai.
- `SIGHUP` terminal band hone ya session disconnect hone se related hai.
- Normal background jobs logout ke baad terminate ho sakti hain.
- `nohup` process ko `SIGHUP` ignore karne deta hai.
- Output ko log file mein redirect karna best practice hai.
- `pstree` parent aur child process relationship dikhata hai.
- Kuch applications `SIGHUP` receive karke configuration reload karti hain.
- Simple persistent jobs ke liye `nohup` theek hai, jab ke production services ke liye `systemd` use karna chahiye.

